{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (-0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The central hole carries an H7 fit tolerance band of only 0.018 mm, but the drawing specifies a zinc plating surface treatment with no allowance for coating thickness. The added plating will push the bore out of its H7 limits and prevent the mating shaft from assembling. The designer must either increase the pre-plating bore size to leave room for the coating or add a note requiring re-machining/masking after plating."
    ,
    "recommended_correction":"Allow for plating thickness on the ⌀16 H7 bore by adjusting the pre-plate machining dimension or specifying post-plate rework."}]}
